package ReviewCenter {
    part def ReviewService {
        doc /* Creates draft reviews from uploaded files or from the changes between two revisions of a registered git repository, freezing the changed content, enforcing the review and upload rules, and reads reviews back. Requires that the actor may see the project (`IProjectAccess`) before creating a review, and takes the repository only from the same project. Records the creator of a review and whether an actor that came through a personal access token created it, naming the token id in the audit entry. Also reads one file back as a line diff between its baseline and head content (`GetDiffAsync`), computed by `LineDiff`. Holds the optional due date of a review (a UTC calendar day, not part of the record digest): checks it at creation, tells whether a review is overdue (`IsOverdue`, and `ListApprovedWithPastDueDateAsync`, which names the approved reviews among those with a past date in one batch for a list), and lets a project or system administrator or the creator, but never an actor of a token, change or clear it on a review that is not approved (`SetDueDateAsync`, audited as `review.due-date-changed`). Also creates a follow-up review of an earlier review of the same project (`followsReviewId`): checks that it fits and carries over the Pass and not-applicable answers, the not-applicable sections, and the open threads (`FollowUpCarry`), all in the same save as the review. Tells, without writing anything, what such a follow-up would carry for a set of files (`PreviewFollowUpAsync`, a result of type `FollowUpPreview`). */

        comment sourceRef /* Source: src/DemaConsulting.ReviewCenter.Core/ReviewService.cs, FollowUpCarry.cs, FollowUpPreview.cs, ReviewCarryOver.cs, Review.cs, ReviewFile.cs, ReviewState.cs, RepositoryReviewResult.cs, and UploadedFile.cs */
        comment testRef /* Test: test/DemaConsulting.ReviewCenter.Tests/Core/ReviewServiceTests.cs, ReviewServiceRepositoryTests.cs, ReviewServiceChecklistTests.cs, ReviewServiceDueDateTests.cs, ReviewServiceFollowUpTests.cs, and FollowUpCarryTests.cs */
        comment designRef /* Design: docs/design/review-center/core/review-service.md */
        comment verificationRef /* Verification: docs/verification/review-center/core/review-service.md */
        comment reqRef /* Requirements: docs/reqstream/review-center/core/review-service.yaml */
    }
}
